  "facts": [
    "The Greenpoint Avenue Bridge, officially the J. J. Byrne Memorial Bridge, opened in 1987 after replacing a 1929 structure plagued by mechanical failures, earning an American Institute of Steel Construction Award in 1991.",
    "On March 30, 2009, Mayor Michael Bloomberg announced a $6 million federal stimulus package at the Greenpoint Avenue Bridge to fund its rehabilitation, a pivotal moment in its modern history.",
    "The bridge’s 2015 completion of a bike lane extension—proposed in 2011—made it the first New York City drawbridge to feature a continuous bike path from Brooklyn across Newtown Creek into Queens."
